  The application itself is a single-page build. GitHub Pages answers a deep
  app route (/tasks, /matrix, ...) with the site's 404.html and a 404 status, so
  listing those routes here would submit URLs a crawler records as not found.
  Only addresses that really answer 200 are listed.

  The guides and the policy pages are static HTML files under public/, so they
  are real 200 responses and are listed individually. The application routes are
  documented for assistants in llms.txt, which does not depend on HTTP status.

  `lastmod` is the day the public copy last changed, not the day the build ran.
-->
